cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "PhysisML: a language model trained from scratch on a developmental curriculum, with dream consolidation against catastrophic forgetting"
abstract: >-
  PhysisML is a language model implemented from scratch (decoder-only
  transformer, forward and backward passes hand-written in NumPy, with a
  PyTorch mirror) and trained on a thirteen-level developmental curriculum of
  Italian, with a dynamic vocabulary and a rule-based tutor so the whole
  curriculum reproduces offline. Each session ends in a dream: a replay
  consolidation pass that turns ~20% cross-level retention into ~88%.
  Benchmarked head-to-head on the same harness, the dream dominates online
  EWC on both seeds (64.4% vs 13.0% final-row retention), with EWC landing
  below the no-protection floor because at near-zero loss the empirical
  Fisher measures inter-example variance on shared structural tokens.
